URL is ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/IAS/sys_check/
Latest version is 1.11.
> 
> >
> > 2) On AIX, I can list devices easily with a command called lsdev ...I need
> > to find out the number and size of the disks in the machine.
> >
> > Any help is appreciated...TIA
> >
> > --Jim
> >
> Try as root:
> 
> file /dev/rrz*c

Doesn't help for RAID controllers (use /dev/rre*c), and even for SCSI
drives
doesn't return the sizes. Personally, I'd also try

uerf -r 300

to get the list of devices found at boot time. Then the results of "df"
and
"disklabel" will give you a handle on what is present. sys_check will of
course
produce all this information.

Regards,
John Hill
