Jim wrote:
> 
> I'm unfamiliar with Digital Unix.  I am however an AIX veteran, so as simple
> as this question is I must proclaim my ignorance towards Digital UNIX is a
> problem, but not UNIX in general..>Oh...that having been said,  is there
> more to adding a TTY in digital unix than just adding a line in the inittab?
> The tty is on serial port 1 on the system, making it tty00 ...do I just add
> a line in the inittab similar to this?
> 
> tty00:234:off:/usr/etc/getty /dev/tty00 2400

Exactly what TTY are you trying to add?

If it is Pseudo TTY for telnet/rlogin, than you're looking in the wrong
direction, you should see

man MAKEDEV

in order to create /dev/pty__ files.

If, on the other hand, you're trynig to add a physical serial TTY, then
you should add a line in /etc/inittab.

> This serial port will be used for connectivity to the UPS ...APCC doesn't
> specify real well about what to put in the inittab.

Aha, APC. Well, if there is no such line, DON'T ADD IT AT ALL. Only if
there is a setting for a (lets say) modem connection, which you would
like to disable, but wouldn't like to delete (so that you don't have to
think it up some time again), then you cahnge "respawn" to "off".

Nix.



