Assuming that the APCC does not actually require a login, you might
not even need an inittab entry. On the otherhand as long as the
specified (default) baud rate is correct then you can not do any
harm and if the APCC code is any good then it will set all of its
own parameters.

> 
> Anyone done this before?  Any help is greatly appreciated.
> 

We use the run_around_the_room_shutdown_now method of dealing with
APCs. Of course the fact that we have not had a power outage since
moving here in 1991 contributes to our sense of irresponsibility.
Heck we do have APCs and some of them are even in use!
