Ain't true. Qlogic distributors (the list is available on the 
Qlogic web site) will gladly sell QLA1040 kits to Joe Public,
including qty 1 purchases. We got one of these cards this way, 
and it was substantially cheaper than KZPBA-CA with all the 
discounts we can get from Digital.

However, I would not recommend the original poster to go this
way: at least some versions of DPW firmware (5.1 for sure)
are very restrictive at identifying PCI devices, and may not
accept some revisions of QLA1040 as KZPBA-CA. If this is the
case, the card can still be made to work once DU boots by
supplying DU driver with the ISP firmware (see alpha-osf-managers
archives at http://www.ornl.gov/its/archives/mailing-lists/ for
instructions), but if that QLA1040 is the only SCSI controller 
in the system, it is of little help.

The problem *may* have been fixed in recent DPW firmware releases,
but I would certainly inquire as to the return policy before
bying QLA1040 for the a->au conversion.

Regards,

/Serge.P



