olivierrobert@minitel.net (Olivier ROBERT) writes:
>Is it possible to create a hard link to a directory?

It's not a good idea anyway because you can put some things like "find" into
infinite loops.  The filesystem is supposed to be a tree and some programs
rely on that.

You'll also find that fsck will "fix" it.

>I need this because I want to grant access to a user in a directory
>which belongs to another user in the same group, but I don't want
>everyone in the group to be able to access to that directory.

Then make a new group.  Users can be in multiple groups.


Someone suggested giving them the same uid.  This is a very bad idea.  Giving
two accounts the same uid basically makes them the same account.  Group
access is precisely what groups are for.



